Verify and scientifically test a substantial computational metallurgical argument (@metal-computational-project: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @metals-and-metallurgical-production, #source "../sources/Pycalphad-Methods-and-Documentation.lingua#r_24VWE1JCTVHMZ88907VK19ZWZR", #source "../sources/Wheeler-Boettinger-McFadden-Phase-Field.lingua#r_32N0NAN7NS30RXD9H2ZSJB81QA", #source "../sources/Quantitative-Phase-Field-Echebarria-and-Colleagues.lingua#r_20GWASGRYTPEAN3V8S54VRZ3GS", #source "../sources/Metals-Alloys-and-Graduate-Teaching-Bhadeshia.lingua#r_0HZJKN8WC6SEWA0DABM8P4HC3F", #source "../../../../inquiry/reproducible-computation/Reproducible-computation.lingua#r_78FWWJDCV0ZGG7VYSPRCWN56DQ", #metals-and-metallurgical-production "Advanced-performance-failure-and-corrective-evidence-study.lingua#r_6GM4DMN4X8E248D3HPH49BM2JE") { r_0E448VGEFYX25TKXHWXRW2E2GB
**Read:** [pycalphad — Otis and Liu, paper and computational thermodynamics](../sources/Pycalphad-Methods-and-Documentation.lingua#r_24VWE1JCTVHMZ88907VK19ZWZR), the complete paper and all exact model/data/solver documentation used; [A Phase-Field Model for Isothermal Phase Transitions in Binary Alloys — NISTIR 4662](../sources/Wheeler-Boettinger-McFadden-Phase-Field.lingua#r_32N0NAN7NS30RXD9H2ZSJB81QA), the full original report and derivations; [Quantitative Phase-Field Model of Alloy Solidification — Echebarria and colleagues](../sources/Quantitative-Phase-Field-Echebarria-and-Colleagues.lingua#r_20GWASGRYTPEAN3V8S54VRZ3GS), the complete paper/preprint, analysis, and validation; [Metals, alloys, steels, and graduate modeling — Bhadeshia teaching materials](../sources/Metals-Alloys-and-Graduate-Teaching-Bhadeshia.lingua#r_0HZJKN8WC6SEWA0DABM8P4HC3F), the full relevant graduate modeling work; [Reproducible computational work](../../../../inquiry/reproducible-computation/Reproducible-computation.lingua#r_78FWWJDCV0ZGG7VYSPRCWN56DQ), reuse the complete verification/reproducibility and numerical/stochastic programme.

Begin with the three original small examples and reproduce their independent references: exact charge balances/optimal endpoints, analytic and discrete Fourier diffusion, and equilibrium/Scheil solute limits. Then choose a consequential alloy-equilibrium, diffusion/transformation, or solidification/interface question requiring a larger model. Read the complete original method and exact software/database documentation used.

For thermodynamic work, inspect phase models, references, fitting/validation evidence, database rights/versions, equilibria, and global-stability assumptions. For phase-field work, read the full NIST report and the complete quantitative alloy-solidification paper, derive conservation and interface relations, and explain the intended thin/sharp-interface limit and model applicability. External implementations are evaluated through their actual versions and methods.

Independently check reduced/analytic cases, material/energy or charge constraints as applicable, positivity, conditioning, temporal/spatial/parameter convergence, sensitivity, and failure behavior. Separate numerical correctness, physical-model adequacy, calibration, and validation with independent observations. A detailed output field or visual pattern cannot prove all four.

**Work:** reproduce a substantial published result, compare with an independent method or limiting calculation, and test a competing physical explanation under changed conditions. Quantify uncertainty and identify the observation that would most change the model choice. Preserve original calculations, environment/version definitions, and the complete external bibliography/data provenance without bundling source software or datasets into the trail.

**Continue:** [Investigate a material or component failure with competing causal explanations and validated correction](Advanced-performance-failure-and-corrective-evidence-study.lingua#r_6GM4DMN4X8E248D3HPH49BM2JE).

**Return:** [Metals and metallurgical production — feed, refining, structure, useful products, and recovery](../Metals-and-metallurgical-production.lingua#r_59BDAQXT81552YF5F8TH4KQQH1).
